# backup-minio bootstrap

1. Make sure the drive is mounted at `/run/media/mugiwara/munin` on the k3s
   node before this pod starts (it uses a hostPath volume, not a PVC, so
   nothing auto-mounts it). `velero-backups/` is created under it on first
   run if missing.

2. Create the root credentials Secret out-of-band (never committed):

   ```
   kubectl create namespace homelab-backup-minio
   kubectl -n homelab-backup-minio create secret generic backup-minio-secrets \
     --from-literal=MINIO_ROOT_USER=<pick-a-username> \
     --from-literal=MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=<pick-a-strong-password>
   ```

3. After ArgoCD syncs (or `helm upgrade --install backup-minio helm/backup-minio -n homelab-backup-minio --create-namespace`),
   create the bucket Velero will use. Easiest from a temporary pod with the
   `mc` client, or port-forward the S3 port and use `mc` locally:

   ```
   kubectl -n homelab-backup-minio port-forward svc/backup-minio 9000:9000 &
   mc alias set backup-minio http://localhost:9000 <MINIO_ROOT_USER> <MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD>
   mc mb backup-minio/velero-local
   ```

4. See `helm/velero/.setup` for wiring this bucket up as Velero's `local`
   BackupStorageLocation.
